<title>INDIA: Philips India 96 net dip to 80 mln rupees.</title>
<headline>Philips India 96 net dip to 80 mln rupees.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical equipment maker Philips India Ltd's net profit fell sharply to 80 million rupees ($22 million) in calendar year 1996 compared with 230 million in 1995, the Press Trust of India (PTI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Philips India Ltd is a subsidary of Philips Electronics NV.</p>
<p>PTI quoted the chief executive officer of Philips India K. R. Ehrnreich as saying that the dip in the profit was due to sluggish market conditions and a high interest burden.</p>
<p>It gave no other details. ($1 = 35.8 rupees)</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
</text>
